  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "lipid-composition-c3e1",
  "summary": "Automated and transferable coarse-grained models now extend to glycans, membranes and filament assembly in recent simulation studies.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is reduced-resolution simulation used to resolve how proteins assemble and interact with their surroundings. A shape-based rigid-body model of human liver PFKL tetramers, with interface-specific interaction sites, simulates filament assembly, while multiscale atomistic and coarse-grained MD with trajectory decomposition maps a multivalent, aromatic-driven self-association pathway for Histatin 1. Coarse-grained MD of ten channel and transporter monomers and oligomers in POPC bilayers links oligomeric interfaces to reduced membrane defects and oligomerization type. GlycoMarinate extends this approach to glycans by automating Martini 3 modelling of N-glycoproteins with transferable and refined glycan models. The information-theoretic analysis of PrPC simulations is a methodological complement rather than a coarse-grained model. What is new is the breadth of environments handled by automated or transferable coarse-grained models, spanning glycans, membranes and protein assemblies.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
